-origin-auth.ts` (session established client-side the instant the key is derived ⇒ login works with zero backend dependency); header/profile/YoroAuthGate/sign-in drive the in-app flow. **Worker** `verifyCacao` = primary control-proof + new `com.etzhayyim.authz.registerAccount` verify-only CACAO relay (gated 202) + CORS. **(c) kotoba account-publish** root-caused+fixed+PROVEN: `kg.ingest` already accepts member-CACAO writes; the one blocker was `kotoba-auth verify_with_resolver` resolving every EdDSA issuer via IPNS/IPFS (a fresh member did:key hangs) — `kotoba-patches/0001-cacao-self-resolve-did-key.patch` short-circuits did:key to `verify_signature()`; proven on an isolated build (`ok:true, quadCount:6`). **Verified**: worker tsc + 12 auth tests green; **live prod** verifyCacao `valid:true` / re-login determinism / tamper-401 / cross-origin-403 / registerAccount-202; **real browser (Chromium 148 + virtual passkey)** — 新規登録 runs the in-app flow (no authn redirect), same-origin verifyCacao+registerAccount, derives a did:key, **UI flips to signed-in**. Merged to `main` for durability. **Account write path (LIVE, content-addressed, NO KV)**: account records are NOT written to a central node (operator-local, ADR-2606013200; `kotobase.net` = IPFS pin service); they are **member-signed content-addressed blocks** published to the apex `com.etzhayyim.apps.kotoba.block.put` and **IPFS-pinned via `kotobase.net`** as the canonical store (the apex KV is only a fast feed cache, never the source of truth — substrate boundary, no centralized DB). Proven live (`block.put` → `{ok:true}`). The **read side** fetches by CID from IPFS + `resolveAccountFromBlock` (re-verify CID + self-certifying handle-attestation) — no KV. ZERO invariant amendments. Honest R0: the mutable handle→CID pointer (kotoba Datom log / DID doc / L2 anchor, never KV) + enrollDevice/rotateKey settings-UI + non-PRF cross-device + PDS PoP-write are follow-ons. | accepted | 2026-06-06 |\n| [2606060900](./2606060900-t