igiri (ADR-2605262700) / hanrei / manabi / baien-distill** — sibling of ADR-2605262400 (geo / netreg / routing / dns / web buckets); adds the `law/` bucket family: `statutes/<jurisdiction>/` + `cases/<court>/` + `treaties/<corpus>/` + `procedures/<body>/` + `templates/<corpus>/` + `commentary/<source>/`. **5 sensor families** under `kotodama.organism.sensors.legal.*`: LegalStatuteSensor (per jurisdiction; statute_class enum) / LegalCaseSensor (per court system, with judicial-party redactor) / LegalTreatySensor (per corpus) / LegalProcedureSensor (per regulatory body) / LegalTemplateSensor (chigiri-consumable templates; structurally separate from raw-law per G6 to avoid sub-licensing/UPL drift). **W1 anchor sensors (5)**: us_usc_sensor + us_cfr_sensor + jp_egov_sensor + eu_eurlex_sensor + uk_legislation_sensor. **License ladder**: Tier-A dominates (most law is public-domain or open-government-license: US public-domain / OGL v3.0 / Étalab / CC0 / ICRC public / EU free-reuse / JP e-Gov CC-BY 4.0); Tier-B for CanLII / AustLII / Indian Kanoon (mixed CC, `-tierB-` infix per G5); **NO proprietary commentary** — Westlaw / LexisNexis / Bloomberg Law / Wolters Kluwer **CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED** per Charter Rider §2(e) anti-gatekeeping + §2(c) covert-ops vendor concern (vendor closed query-tracking exposes member legal posture). Tier-C limited to NEVER in W1 (future ADR + Council Lv6+ for NC commentary). **Sources covered (~30)**: US (USC / CFR / Federal Register / FRCP-FRCrP-FRE / CAP Harvard CC0 / CourtListener / RECAP-PACER) / UK (legislation.gov.uk / Find Case Law TNA / GOV.UK procedures) / EU (EUR-Lex statutes+CJEU) / JP (e-Gov 法令 / 裁判所 判例 / 官報 / 国税庁 通達) / Council of Europe (ECHR HUDOC) / UN (Treaty Collection / UNCITRAL / WIPO / Hague Conference / ILO 180+) / ICRC (Geneva Conventions + APs) / DE (BGBl) / FR (Légifrance Étalab) / IT (Normattiva) / KR (KLIC) / CA (CanLII Tier-B) / AU (AustLII Tier-B) / IN (India Code + Indian Kanoon Tier-B) / BR (Senate + STJ) / CN (NPC, §2(g) state-aligned flag) / ICJ + ICC public / OECD / NIST SP800 / CoE handbooks / Apache 2.0 + CC license corpora. **Judicial-party redaction policy** (per-jurisdiction): pass-through where parties named in upstream publication (US/UK/IN/BR/CA/AU/ICJ/ICC); pass-through-pseudonymized where upstream pseudonymized (DE/FR/JP/CN/IT/KR); honor upstream anonymization (ECHR HUDOC); reject if non-anonymized (JP 家庭裁判所 / 少年裁判所). chigiri does NOT re-identify or de-anonymize; right-to-be-forgotten DSARs route through chigiri.data_privacy cell to upstream publisher, never unilateral removal. **5 training corpus recipes** at `70-tools/baien-moemoekyun-train/recipes/legal/`: legal-foundations-r1 / chigiri-procedural-r1 / ihl-defensive-r1 / manabi-legal-literacy-r1 / tax-receipt-multi-juris-r1 (all Tier-A, publishable). **2 new Kaizen rules**: R10 (statute-staleness >90d for active jurisdictions / >365d for slow-revision sources) + R11 (case-law jurisdiction-drift: cited statutes pinned-stale rate >20% triggers re-pull). **14 gates G1..G14** (Charter scan + PII filter + judicial-party redactor + replicationMin:2 + cadence vs upstream + tier-B infix + template/raw-law separation G6 + Murakumo-only G7 + no-active-probe G8 incl Westlaw/Lexis/Bloomberg deny-list + hot_sample determinism + recipe in git G10 + FP ≤5%/24h + datasetPin mandatory + legal-corpus-manifest append). **12 non-goals N1..N12**: N1 not a commercial legal-research substitute / N2 not live scraping / N3 not de-anonymization tool / N4 not vendor-feed integrator (Westlaw/Lexis/Bloomberg PROHIBITED) / N5 not legal-advice generator (UPL via chigiri G14) / N6 not court-filing system / N7 not paywall-bypass / N8 not contract-drafting AI / N9 not human-counsel substitute / N10 not cross-religious-corp federation / N11 not substrate engine replacement / N12 not vendor-LLM inference. **5-wave delivery**: W0 = this ADR + sensor scaffold + recipe templates / W1 = 5 anchor sources (US USC + CFR + UK legislation + EU EUR-Lex +