ed patch generation/submission is out of scope for akuma\"). Takes an owner-attested vulnerability **finding** → synthesizes a **defensive fix patch** → validates in an egress-restricted sandbox → **proposes** it to the authorized target (fork-and-PR / signed patch bundle). **Deliberately separated pair**: akuma = offensive-diagnosis (no write); tsukuroi = defensive-remediation (no probe, propose-only) — distinct egress namespaces are the security boundary. **RemediationMandate** contract parallels akuma's scope contract: `finding_cid` (upstream akuma finding) + `allowed_paths[]` + `submission_mode` {fork-pr, patch-file, config-diff} + owner+authority dual signature + `delegation_credential_ref` (owner-issued least-privilege expiring fork-PR-only credential, vault ciphertext — never a platform-held key) + `mergeAuthorityHeld` const false. **13 gates G1..G13**: G1 Charter Rider §2(a)..(h) scan / G2 kotoba datom append-only / **G3 NO PROBING** (input via akuma finding_cid only; negative-space) / **G4 PROPOSE-ONLY / NO AUTONOMOUS MERGE** (`mergeAuthorityHeld`+`autonomousMerge` const false; `autonomousMergeCount=0`) / **G5 DEFENSIVE-ONLY / NO EXPLOIT** (§2(a); `defensiveOnly` const true; `exploitArtifactCount=0`) / G6 scoped write (`pathsTouched ⊆ allowedPaths`) / G7 dual-sig mandate / **G8 NO PLATFORM-HELD KEY** (ADR-2605231525; `platformHeldKeyCount=0`) / G9 sandbox validation never against live target (`ranAgainstLiveTarget` const false) / G10 Murakumo-only inference (ADR-2605215000) / G11 closure requires akuma re-probe pass + owner human merge / G12 rate limit / G13 Bonsai seed-tier prune on unauthorized write. **12 non-goals N1..N12** (N1 NOT a scanner=akuma / N2 NOT autonomous deploy / N3 NOT merge-bot / N4 NOT exploit generator / N5 NOT commercial patch-SaaS — Snyk Fix / GHAS-paid / Mend / Veracode / Checkmarx / Black Duck PROHIBITED §2(e), OSS only / N6 NOT key-holder / N7 NOT mandate-less / N8 NOT out-of-scope write / N9 NOT a human-review substitute / N10 NOT