ion of 7 candidates (IPFS-optimized / Tahoe-LAFS / Storj / Sia / Fireproof / generic-DHT / in-house) across 8 criteria. **Both maximin and weighted sum select `kotoba-dht`** (weighted 8.30 ≫ Fireproof 7.20 > Storj 6.45 > Tahoe 6.15 > IPFS=DHT 5.55 > Sia 5.50; maximin worst-dimension 5 vs 2–3). **Decision**: (D1) durability + proof-of-retention owner = the already-scaffolded `kotoba-dht` validating DHT (`neighborhood` XOR-distance r-replication + `availability_proof` epoch challenge reward≥0.80/slash<0.50 + `warrant` invalidity gossip + `source_chain` per-agent append-only = Datomic accretion-isomorphic, mutable head = chain tip NOT IPNS); (D2) **IPFS demoted to CIDv1 cold/interop backstop only** — sharpens ADR-2605312345 \"IPFS=block backend\" by naming the owner of the guarantee IPFS never gave; (D3) `NeighborhoodBlockStore` slots into the existing `TieredBlockStore` where the Kubo cold tier sits (hot=Budgeted/Memory · durability=Neighborhood · cold/interop=Kubo · anchor=Base L2); (D4) **Holochain architecture AFFIRMED but realized inside the kotoba workspace (`kotoba-dht`), NOT the deprecated kotoba-datomic protocol family** (kotoba-datomic name + 10-protocol/kotoba-datomic/ stay superseded by 2605262130); (D5) `availability_proof` reward/slash settles in **USDC on Base L2 (ADR-2605172100), NO foreign storage token** — the decisive reason Storj (STORJ) / Sia (Siacoin) / token-mandatory networks were rejected despite strong durability. Token-mandatory networks are structurally penalized on the Charter C6 axis regardless of reweighting unless the USDC-on-Base invariant is dropped. Fireproof's local-first prolly-CRDT pattern retained as the embedded read/merge layer (validates kotoba's own prolly design) but not as the durability network. **Honest**: highest one-time build cost; `kotoba-dht` unproven at scale (r / churn / slash-economics need empirical tuning); Base L2 incentive contract Council-ratify-gated (design-only). No data migration (CIDv1 identical across ti