e each already covered — EDN gives keyword/set/instant semantics, CBOR gives compact IPLD-canonical binary — so it's a 3rd redundant format (against Shannon-minimality, ADR-2604251830). Two hard blockers: (1) **dag-cbor CID lock-in** — CIDs are SHA2-256 over dag-cbor bytes; content-addressing + IPFS *require* dag-cbor in the block layer, Transit can't replace it without breaking CID/IPFS compat; (2) **weak Rust support** — Transit is Clojure-centric, no maintained production Rust codec, kotoba is Rust-first. **Narrow documented exception (NOT adopted)**: Transit-JSON on the HTTP wire is the one place it could help (keyword/set fidelity over a JSON-compatible transport + key-caching on large attribute-repetitive result sets, polyglot Datomic-client compat) — reconsider only if a Datomic-compatible polyglot client protocol is required, and even then benchmark vs cheaper substitutes (EDN-over-wire, `application/cbor` body [codec present], zstd on JSON). Depends on ADR-2606012000 + 2605312345 + 2605262130 + 2604251830. | accepted | 2026-06-01 |\n| [2606012101](./2606012101-okaimono-provisioning-commons-actor.md) | **okaimono 御買物 — global product-discovery + provisioning-commons actor (`okaimono.etzhayyim.com`)** — the charter-aligned answer to *\"build an Amazon-like service inside etzhayyim.\"* A naïve port is **unbuildable**: Amazon's three pillars are constitutional prohibitions (external `purchase` value-inflow §1.3 / ads + affiliate Charter-Rider §2 / engagement dark-patterns §1.13) and the 反個人主義/多世代 ontology. okaimono **inverts** Amazon — each prohibited term replaced by its charter dual — into a *provisioning commons* of **three concentric rings**: **Ring 0 commons-first** (borrow/share · repair→hodoki · durable-secondhand · surplus→UNSPSC-organism `surplus-routing` — \"the best purchase is no purchase\", the Wellbecoming inversion of \"buy more\"); **Ring 1 internal economy** (full list→compare→basket→checkout over etzhayyim's own ~30 producing actors mitsuho/ma