1525); did:web canonical (ADR-2605212030). Verified: worker tsc + 15 tests; runner 6; ameno tsc + 9; kanae runs; real ipfs CAR reassembles; keccak vectors; self-cert chain on kanae's real CID. **Next steps**: IPNS mutable-pointer transport (whole path self-certifying); mesh-runner libp2p transport; register actor ed25519 keys in the seed; operator enablement (enable-kv + `--pin-did` + pin attestations + `IPFS_GATEWAYS` + ERC725 deploy). Authoritative designs = ADR-2606015200 + 2606015400 + 2606015600. | active | 2026-06-02 |\n| [2606015600](./2606015600-self-certifying-did-attestation.md) | **Self-certifying DID-document attestation (did:key signs the did.json CID)** — makes the handle→CID binding **trustless**, completing IPFS-based DID retrieval (ADR-2606015400). The remaining gap there was that the binding was anchored only by `etzhayyim.com` TLS; now each actor's did.json is bound to its CID by a signature from the actor's **own ed25519 key, expressed as a `did:key`** — verification is self-certifying (the key IS the identifier, no external anchor). `src/diddoc-attest.ts` (worker, **verify-only**): base58btc + `did:key` derivation (`ed25519PubToDidKey`/`didKeyToEd25519Pub`, multicodec `0xed01`) + `verifyDidDocAttestation` (WebCrypto Ed25519); the server NEVER signs (ADR-2605231525). Attestation = `{did, didDocCid, signedAt, sequence, proof:{Ed25519Signature2020, verificationMethod: did:key:z…, proofValue: z…}}`. `scripts/sign-diddoc.mjs` (operator tool): the actor/operator's own key signs the canonical did.json CID; private key never the server's. `toDidDoc` adds `did:key:<publicKeyMultibase>` to `alsoKnownAs` when the actor has an `Ed25519VerificationKey2020` vm, cross-linking handle↔key. **Trustless chain**: `did:key:z6Mk…` → verify attestation sig → trust `didDocCid` → fetch + CID-verify did.json from any IPFS gateway → confirm `doc.id` + that it lists the `did:key`; **TLS no longer required for the binding**. Verified end-to-end: signing tool produced a `did:key` + attestation binding kanae's real did.json CID; `verifyDidDocAttestation` confirmed it. Worker tsc + **15 tests** (5 attestation, 3 did-doc-cid, 4 car, 3 erc725). **Honest R0**: ships the signed attestation (key→CID); the **IPNS** mutable-pointer transport (latest CID under the key's name, no TLS) is next; no DID-method change (did:web canonical, did:key alias+signer); actors' keys not yet in the seed (`vm:[]`) — registering each `Ed25519VerificationKey2020` is operator work (demo generates a key); pinning the attestation operator-gated. Depends on ADR-2606015400 + 2606013800 + 2605212030 + 2605231525. | accepted | 2026-06-02 |\n| [2606015400](./2606015400-mesh-runner-serving-and-ipfs-did-retrieval.md) | **Mesh-runner serving surface + IPFS-based DID retrieval** — two follow-ups to ADR-2606015200. **(D1)** `e7m-wasm-runner/serve.mjs` turns the T2 runner into a real HTTP service: `GET /xrpc/com.etzhayyim.actor.run?actor=<did\\|handle>` + `/healthz` → resolve → CID/CAR-verify → run (core or jco component) → JSON, **cached by CID**; 3 tests (real http vs stub gateway). **(D2)** answers *「did を IPFS ベースでの取得にできる?」* → **yes**: did:web stays canonical (TLS trust anchor) but every actor's `did.json` is now **content-addressed**. `canonicalDidDoc`/`didDocCid` (`actor-profiles.ts`) normalize the one request-volatile field (`_meta.source`) so the **CID is stable across KV/kotoba/compiled tiers**; `/actor/<h>/did.json` advertises `x-etzhayyim-did-doc-cid` + `Link: rel=canonical`, `/.well-known/actors.json` lists `didDocumentCid`/`didDocumentIpfs`/`didDocumentGateway`. A client gets the authentic CID from `etzhayyim.com` (TLS), then fetches + verifies the did.json from **any IPFS gateway** (apex `/ipfs/<cid>` or third-party). Publisher materializes + pins (`--pin-did`); **worker (TS) and publisher (JS) compute byte-identical canonical did.json CIDs** (verified tsumugi/kanae/watatsuna via an esbuild-bundled cross-check). Verified: worker tsc + 10 tests; runner 6 tests. **Honest R0**: handle→CID binding still anchored by `etzhayyim.com` TLS (full did:ipfs/IPNS self-certifying = future); pinning + serving from the etzhayyim pin operator-gated; libp2p transport not yet wired (HTTP is the bridge); CID changes on did.json change (re-pin). Depends on ADR-2606015200 + 2606014600 + 2606013800 + 2605212030 + 2605231525. | accepted | 2026-06-02 |\n| [2606015200](./2606015200-wasm-actor-runtime-round-2-dagpb-mesh-kanae-erc725.md) | **WASM-actor runtime round 2 — dag-pb CAR verify + mesh runner + kanae T1 + ameno panel + ERC725 mirror + operator runbook** — lands all six next-steps from ADR-2606014800 in one PR. **(2)** `src/car.ts`: CARv1 parse + per-block sha2-256 verify + UnixFS reassembly → multi-block **dag-pb (`bafybei…`) content is now trustless** too; `/ipfs/<cid>` fetches `?format=car` for dag-pb and serves reconstructed bytes (verified vs a real 620 KB `ipfs dag export` CAR + 4 unit tests incl. tamper-rejection). **(6)** `50-infra/e7m-wasm-runner` — T2 mesh node: resolve → CID/CAR-verify → run core (`WebAssembly.instantiate`) or component (`jco`); 3 tests. **(1)** new T1 actor **kanae 鼎** (`20-actors/kanae/wasm/kanae-core`, Rust→wasm 23.9 KB, raw CID, fiscal-flow top-recipient = Prefectures, NON-adjudicating) registered (`did:web:etzhayyim.com:actor:kanae`) → proves the T1 path generalizes. **(3)** `@etzhayyim/ameno/inference/wasm-actor-panel` `mountActorPanel()` + pure `formatActorResult` + runnable `demo/wasm-actor.html`; ameno tsc clean + 7 tests. **(5)** `src/erc725.ts` — own `keccak256` (known-vector tested) + gated `fetchOnChainVm` reads `resolveDwebHandle(keccak256(handle.etzhayyim.com))` via `eth_call` → secp256k1 vm mirror, wired into `resolveActorRecord` (best-effort, [] until contract live; never server-minted). **(4)** `scripts/enable-kv.sh` (`npm run enable-kv`) + `RUNBOOK.md` (KV/kotoba/IPFS_GATEWAYS/ERC725/mesh). Verified: worker tsc + 7 tests; runner 3; ameno tsc + 7; kanae runs; ipfs CAR reassembles exactly. **Honest R