argo-shipbuilding.md) | **Session close — funadaiku 船大工 zero-emission cargo shipbuilding (R0 + kami-engine operational voyage sim)** — documentation-only closure for the 2026-06-01 session per ADR-2606013400. Shipped: R0 actor `20-actors/funadaiku/` (manifest/CLAUDE/README + 9 Pregel cells import-clean RuntimeError-on-`.solve()` + 9 lexicons `com.etzhayyim.funadaiku.*` integer-typed gate-clean) + **Nagi 凪 class** `vessel.edn` (wind + solar + H₂ fuel cell + LFP + e-pod, **no fossil engine** G13/N5) + `shipyard.edn` (ATEX H₂ bay + routed MEP, giemon-factory pattern) + `building.edn` SBOM + `fleet.kotoba.edn` yard robots + `products.edn` (okaimono Ring-1) + analytic `methods/voyage_energy.py` (200 nm: **wind 16.0% / solar 1.9% / hydrogen 82.1% / fossil 0.0%**). **Operational sim**: `kami-autodrive/examples/nagi_voyage.rs` sails the Nagi autonomously (Autopilot+ShipHydro GNC) on a zero-emission powertrain that gates thrust (no fossil; throttle power-limited, not fuel-topped) → captured arrival **hydrogen 84.4% / solar 8.9% / wind 6.6% / fossil 0.0%** (`out/nagi-voyage-sim.txt`); `tests/nagi_zero_emission_voyage.rs` 2 green + full kami-autodrive suite green + examples build. Verified: py_compile clean; JSON valid; EDN round-trips; `voyage_energy.py` runs; cargo test/build green; lefthook green (lexicon number→integer fix + registry/graph regen). Registered in root CLAUDE.md table + adr/README + deps.toml. **Honest**: R0 design+data-model+sim only; no steel cut; ShipHydro small-vessel surrogate at perception-grid scale (shares scale-invariant, kWh demo-scale; 6-DOF CFD R2+); coastal scale (ocean VLCC out of R0–R3, G12); `:representative`; live yard/bunkering/sea-trial Council+operator gated. Delivered on `feat/funadaiku-zero-emission-cargo-shipbuilding` (2887a6789 R0 + 29af5fe13 sim) → PR #681; concurrent `feat/sarutahiko` branch transiently carried a stray sim-commit copy, canonical copy moved cleanly via isolated worktree (no force-push). Authoritative design = ADR-2606013400. Depends on ADR-2606013400 + 2606010600 + 2605252200. | active | 2026-06-01 |\n| [2606014500](./2606014500-one-worker-wasm-actor-model.md) | **One Worker, many WASM actors** — answers *「CF Worker は etzhayyim.com のみにして、他の actor は IPFS/他 protocol、kotoba は WASM なのでブラウザで読み込んで local 実行できる?」*. **Yes — the natural endpoint of the existing trajectory.** Per-actor CF Workers were already collapsed to one (ADR-2605241800 Phase A); the residue was the `https://<actor>.etzhayyim.com` `#xrpc-https-legacy` host entries. **Decision**: `etzhayyim.com` is the ONLY first-party CF Worker (identity / dynamic `did.json` / `/actors` / donate / apex proxy — **no actor compute**). An actor's **state** = kotoba Datom log; its **logic** = a content-addressed **WASM component on IPFS**. **D2** DID doc carries a new `EtzhayyimWasmComponent` service (`ipfs://<cid>`, first) from `:actor/wasm-cid`. **D3** execution tiers, no per-actor server: **T1 browser-local (ameno)** fetch WASM from IPFS → instantiate → run locally (+WebGPU/WebNN); **T2 donated mesh (kotoba/e7m)** via libp2p; **T0 per-actor Worker removed**. **D4 trust** = did:web TLS + WASM **CID integrity** (loader recomputes sha256→CIDv1, refuses mismatched bytes) — **no server key** (ADR-2605231525). **D5** retire all `#xrpc-https-legacy` per-actor hosts (Phase C). **D6** inference Murakumo-only / ameno frozen-edge. **PoC shipped (tsumugi)**: Rust→`wasm32-unknown-unknown` `tsumugi-core` (23.5 KB, edge-primary 取-concentration) → real IPFS CIDv1 `bafkreidftt…kddfi`; `loader/index.html` (browser) + `loader/verify.mjs` (headless, CI-runnable) both **resolve → recompute-CID-integrity → execute locally** asserting top 取 = TSMC; tsumugi did.json carries the WASM service; all 10 actors' legacy HTTPS hosts removed; worker `tsc` clean. **Honest R0**: bounded `:representative` seed (reproduces direction, not exact numbers); core module not yet WASI/Component-Model; libp2p browser dispatch (T2) + live IPFS pinning + `etzhayyim.com/ipfs/<cid>` gateway operator-gated; most Tier-B actors are py langgraph → `componentize-py` migration path. Depends on ADR-2605241800 + 2606013800 + 2606013600 + 2605241900 + 2605231525 + 2605215000 + 2605262130. | accepted | 2026-06-01 |\n| [2606013800](./2606013800-actor-profile-and-dynamic-did-issuance.md) | **Actor profile schema + dynamic did.json issuance from kotoba** — closes two defects: (1) `etzhayyim.com/profile/did:web:...:tsumugi` returned \"profile not found\" because the apex Worker proxies `/profile/*` to yoro, which resolves a **handle** against the PDS, and tsumugi is kotoba-native with **no atproto repo**; (2) `/actor/<h>/did.json` was hardcoded in `infra-actors.ts`, not issued from canonical state. **D1** new SSoT `00-contracts/schemas/actor-profile.kotoba.edn` (`:actor/*` in public `actors-v1` graph) — one record backs BOTH the DID Document AND the `app.bsky.actor.getProfile` view (+ `actor-profile-seed.kotoba.edn` for 10 actors). **D2** dynamic did.json: apex Worker `resolveActorRecord` = **3-tier fail-open** KV (`actor:<handle>`) → kotoba pull (`kg.entity`) → compiled `INFRA_ACTORS` fallback, mapped through pure `toDidDoc()`; `verificationMethod` is a **mirror of on-chain ERC725** (empty today → no server-minted key, ADR-2605231525; did:web trust = TLS). **D3** profile resolution: new `GET /actor/<h>/profile.json` + getProfile XRPC short-circuit for registered actors (human members never hijacked) + yoro SSR `getProfile()` resolves actor DIDs via apex first (additive, PDS fallback) → `/profile/did:web:...:tsumugi` now renders via AgentProfile. **D4** publisher `scripts/publish-actor-records.mjs` (seed EDN → KV `--put-kv` / kotoba `--ingest-kotoba`), mappers mirrored JS/TS so KV/kotoba/compiled render identically. Worker `tsc` clean; publisher verified on tsumugi+watatsuna. **Honest R0**: KV namespace + `KOTOBA_ENDPOINT` operator-gated (kotoba has no public read surface yet); until enabled the Worker serves the compiled fallback through the same mappers (identical output); `kg.entity` consumed defensively; yoro change in the deprecated-but-live appview copy. Demotes the hardcoded DID registry to a fallback; keeps did:web always-live. Depends on ADR-2605212030 + 2605241800 + 2605231525 + 2605312345 + 2605262130 + 2606011800. | accepted | 2026-06-01 |\n| [2606013600](./2606013600-browser-kotoba-node-sovereign-tier2.md) | **Browser kotoba node — kqe-in-wasm as the sovereign client-side apex tier-2** — answers *「kotoba を browser の wasm として動かすことはできないか?」* (and so dissolves *「自前 kotoba ノードをどこにホストするか」*). The apex resolver is 3-tier KV → kotoba → compiled `INFRA_ACTORS` (ADR-2606013800), but **KV is only a 300 s auto-cache of the kotoba pull** (tier-2 writes it back with `expirationTtl: 300`), not a source of truth, and the CF edge is vendor-managed. **Decision**: the `kotoba-wasm` browser node (`kotoba-kqe` EAVT/AEVT/AVET/VAET + CID-verified Prolly traversal compiled to `wasm32`, + client-side `ed25519` `commitSigned` no-server-key write, + `kotoba-store-web` IndexedDB persist) is the **sovereign client-side form of tier-2** — the browser IS the node, the apex Worker is reduced to a content-verifying gateway (`cid.ts`/`car.ts`/`diddoc-attest.ts` already shipped), and **the only durable tier is commodity IPFS pinning**, never a trust/auth root. A browser tab cannot be the Worker's inbound `KOTOBA_ENDPOINT` (no inbound HTTP), but that is moot — client-side read removes the server pull; the sovereign server layering is **2-tier kotoba → compiled**, KV demoted to an optional self-filling cache (manual no-TTL KV pre-seed shadows canonical updates — discouraged). **Empirically verified 2026-06-06** (`50-infra/etzhayyim-did-web/poc-browser-node/`): `kotoba-wasm` → `wasm32` clean (release+wasm-opt **gzip ≈ 790 KB**, within the baien edge envelope; use rustup not Homebrew rust); Node-driven proof on the **REAL 28-actor SSoT** (`actor-profile-seed.kotoba.edn`) resolves `did:web:etzhayyim.com:actor:kamado` client-side + signed content-addressed `commitSigned` + deterministic root (9/9); real **Google Chrome 148** via playwright-core (Service Worker answers `searchActors` from in-browser wasm, `x-kotoba-sw: local-wasm`, kamado resolved, 4/4 + screenshot). ZERO invariant amendments — strengthens kotoba-canonical-state (2605262130/2605312345), no-server-key (2605231525), Murakumo-only (2605215000). Honest R0: artifacts reproducible not committed (no git-lfs); dedicated etzhayyim CF account + standing IPFS pinner are tracked follow-ups; root-canonical record of the id the kotoba submodule crate references. | proposed | 2026-06-06 |\n| [2605312355](./2605312355-session-close-kotoba-datom-first-class-and-charter-rider-d1.md) | **Session close — kotoba Datom first-class state + SHA2-256 CID + Charter Rider D1 applied** — documentation-only closure for the 2026-05-31 session. (1) ADR-2605312345 made the kotoba **Datom log the first-class canonical state** (IPFS=block backend, MST=ingress/interop wire, Base L2=trust anchor). (2) Merged kotoba upstream main into the submodule (51 commits behind), preserving un-upstreamed multimodal work first; **empirically confirmed the CID is unified to a single SHA2-256 CIDv1** (cid.rs `Sha256::digest`; dual-CID/blake3 removed in kotoba `144df21`) — corrected stale Dual-CID docs; kotoba **PR #10** merged (multimodal ADR-2605302200 + LangGraph/WASM fixes); `cargo check --workspace` green. (3) root **PR #301** merged. (4) root **PR #302** re-baselined the subrepo escape-symlink audit 18→0 (the 18 were the kotoba git-subrepo CHARTER-RIDER.md escape symlinks, resolved by the git-subrepo→git-submodule migration — not a regression). (5) **Charter Rider v2.0 applied to kotoba upstream** (kotoba **PR #11** → `ecba123d`: a REAL `CHARTER-RIDER.md` copy + `NOTICE` + README, NOT a dangling `../../` escape symlink since kotoba is standalone; workspace-level covers all crates) + root submodule bump **PR #304** — **ADR-2605262130 D1 now SATISFIED**. Incident post-mortem: a `--no-check