ty = a revocable CACAO leash (member-signed delegation + issuer)** — answers 「app password は kotoba server, actor ではどう設計されているか → 自律的生命としてはどう管理させるのが良い? a改」. kotoba has NO passwords (app-password is an AT-Proto PDS concept the member holds in their own runtime); it is DID-centric (passkey-wrapped keys, Bearer JWT `sub==DID`, CACAO DelegationChain for graph writes). The right identity for an autonomous life the platform may hold no key for (no-server-key, ADR-2605231525) and that has no human present each beat is a SCOPED, EXPIRING, REVOCABLE capability — a **leash**, not a held key. Three custodial roles never collapsed: ISSUE (member, own key, signs `datom:transact@graph:ibuki,exp:+Nd` in their own runtime) / INVOKE (organism PRESENTS the opaque `cacao_b64` every beat — present-only, stdlib, never signs) / REVOKE (`exp` lapses → fail-open; stop re-issuing → it quietly retires). #1593 `methods/delegation.py` (present-only, scope+expiry vs caller `now_epoch`, fail-open) wired into `kotoba_bridge.push(delegation=,now_epoch=)`. #1599 `tools/issue_delegation.py` member-side minting tool (member's OWN runtime; MAY use `cryptography`) → byte-correct CAIP-122/SIWE CACAO (Ed25519 over `siwe_message()`, hand-rolled CBOR). Minting a REAL CACAO against the live node **corrected two assumptions** (both now from `kotoba-auth`): `aud` = the kotoba NODE's operator DID, not the organism's (organism is the BEARER); `write_author` = the issuing MEMBER (autonomous writes on-record attributed to the consenting human — accountability by consent, a better model than 'writes as itself'). LIVE-VERIFIED 2026-06-11: a real member-signed CACAO is parsed + Ed25519-verified reaching DID-resolution; full write-acceptance additionally needs the node's IPFS DID resolver up (operator infra, not a design/actor gap). 242 tests / 21 hermetic stdlib-only suites green. ZERO invariant amendments. | accepted | 2026-06-11 |\n| [2606112000](./2606112000-kotoba-actor-dna-code-data-unification.md) | **Actor DNA — binding kotoba CODE + DATA into one content-addressed unit (Holochain-/Ethereum-iso)** — answers 「ethereum, holochain のように コードとデータが一体化して deploy できているか」. kotoba already content-addresses + re-verifies BOTH code (WASM CID) and data (Datom log/graph CID) — the trustless half — but did not UNIFY them: four separate CIDs linked only by did.json, no code-defined data validation (kg.rs = append-only + CACAO auth, no validate() hook), non-atomic deploy. The **Actor DNA manifest** (`kotoba-actor-dna/v0`) binds `:dna/wasm-cid`(CODE) + `:dna/graph`+`graph-cid`(DATA, derived+re-checked) + `:dna/validation-cid` + `:dna/lexicon-cid` + `:dna/capability`(the ibuki CACAO leash) into ONE raw DNA CID that is the actor's identity — did.json points at `ipfs://<dna-cid>` and nothing else; any part change → new DNA CID → a different actor. + the **integrity ruleset** (`kotoba-integrity/v0`, the Holochain integrity-zome analogue): a content-addressed ruleset + `validate()` that REJECTS non-conforming datoms before push (append-only/closed-vocab/types/deny/required/graph-binding), tamper-evident because the rules are in the actor's hash. + the **deploy descriptor** (every step binds the one DNA CID). `50-infra/actor-dna/` pure-stdlib, **33 tests / 4 suites**; cid byte-identical vs rasen + the live engine graph CID. HONEST: client/actor-tier enforced now; engine-tier validate-before-commit (peer writes) + single-tx atomicity = gated `40-engine/kotoba` follow-up. ZERO invariant amendments. | accepted | 2026-06-11 |\n| [2606111824](./2606111824-session-close-review-merge-wave-adr-id-races.md) | **Session close — review-and-merge wave (7 root PRs + 3 kotoba PRs) + ADR-id race ×2 renumber pattern** — non-authoritative index of the 2026-06-11 review/merge passes: cleanroom L5 wave #1620 (gemini-CLI verified dev-time-only, Murakumo invariant holds) · ehyeh doctrine #1623 · argon2id-v1 KDF #1625 (fail-closed dispatch verified in code) · kaiyaku #1626 + tate #1628 (the two halves of #1624, each **renumbered** out of an ADR-id race — 2606112200→2606112201 vs ehyeh, 2606112300→2606112301 vs mimamori) · the #1618 **unfetchable-gitlink incident** (pinned a local pre-amend object; main unclonable until #1619 repointed to the pushed SHA) · CI submodule series #1617→#1619→#1622 closing the mst-projector tsc + cyber-drill pnpm failures. Normative §3: the **renumber-supersede pattern** for ADR-id races (fresh worktree + cherry-pick + scoped renumber proving zero collateral on same-number references + re-test + supersede with full accounting incl. re-checking the original branch for late commits — tate was pushed mid-supersede and nearly dropped). Prevention recommended: PR-gate uniqueness check on the numeric ADR id + actual-JST-time ids (forward-dating to round numbers manufactured both races). | accepted | 2026-06-11 |\n| [2606111640](./2606111640-portfolio-qa-deflake-coverage-ci-wave.md) | **Portfolio QA wave — SDK quorum-test deflake + kotoba coverage baseline + CI** — the 2026-06-11 maturity audit's verification-layer fixes. (1) `@etzhayyim/sdk` was believed red on the incomplete libsignal→XChaCha20 migration; that note was **stale** — the real failure was a flaky quorum assertion (`minority.toHaveLength(2)` vs `collectQuorum`'s documented threshold early-exit + fire-and-forget in-memory transport ordering); now asserts the guaranteed semantics (matching=3 all-accept, minority ≤2 all-reject), 188 tests ×3 runs green, `sdk-test` green on PR CI; SDK lockfile re-synced (`@noble/hashes ^1.8.0`) (PR #1613). (2) kotoba gains `scripts/coverage.sh` (cargo-llvm-cov, rustup-stable-pinned — Homebrew rust has no llvm-tools) with the **first measured baseline: 78.75% line / 79.37% region / 76.05% fn** (workspace lib tests; low spots recorded honestly: kotoba-clj/-ingest/b2_* 0%, kubo_store 37%, wasm_pregel 47%, signal_xrpc 57%) (kotoba PR #104) + **first CI** (`cargo test --workspace --lib` + rust-cache; explicit host-triple `--target` overrides the repo's aarch64-apple-darwin `.cargo/config.toml` pin on linux runners) (kotoba PR #105). (3) Standing fixture rule: CACAO test fixtures carry far-future `expiry`, never hardcoded `issued_at` + `expiry: None` (7-day `MAX_CACAO_AGE_SECS` date rot — flushed out the `pre_proxy` e2e fixture, silently red since 06-07). Known break surfaced NOT fixed: `tsc (mst-projector)` on main (`yorishiro-huggingface-inference-mcp` declared `workspace:*`, exists nowhere in the monorepo). | accepted | 2026-06-11 |\n| [2606111330](./2606111330-session-close-shionome-t1-wasm-live-did-actor-kotobase-pin.md) | **Session close — 潮目 T1 browser-wasm DID actor LIVE on etzhayyim.com + kotobase.net pin saga (root-caused)** — answers 「https://etzhayyim.com/ で browser wasm, did actor として動いている?」: was **NO on three levels** (fallback-scaffold did.json; ZERO actors' wasm fetchable, apex `/ipfs` 502; only artifact = 18.5MB dag-pb T2), made **YES** via PR #1588 with a **5-step production proof** — DID resolve (`_meta.source kotoba`) → `EtzhayyimWasmComponent` → apex `/ipfs` 200 cid-verified → local CID re-verify MATCH → execute `{regime:risk-on, grand_total:1383tn, no_trade:true}`. **(c)** `shionome-core` Rust T1 wasm (18,762B raw CID, tsumugi/kanae ABI; build asserts `no_trade:true` on the actual wasm output — G2 in the artifact). **(a)** registration in 3 homes (actor-profile-seed + INFRA_ACTORS + static `public/actor/shionome/` — discovery: named actors are edge-served STATIC files; the KV-put path is a no-op for did.json); worker 101/101 tests, deployed `b50b69fb`. **(b)** local-leg pinning (TWO-ipfs-repo decoy found; **kanae's rebuild reproduced its registered CID bit-identically → its 502 FIXED**; tsumugi loader artifact matched) — all 3 T1 actors 200. **kotobase.net leg root-caused, NOT complete**: PSA `/pins` shim → `kotoba-backend.gftd.ai`; tenant duality (hex `ze2e…` vs canonical multibase `z6MktEjt…`); pins registered but stalled — pin worker awaits kubo `pin/add` with **no timeout** + pod `peer_count:0` (operator follow-up: pod connectivity / IpfsPinClient timeout+fallback patch). Honest boundary: durability today = jacob's NAT'd kubo + gateway caches; T2 unpinned; Murakumo down; jacob disk-full incident (user freed 21GiB). ZERO invariant amendments. | accepted | 2026-06-11 |\n| [2606101400](./2606101400-tedai-member-computer-operation-tier-b-actor-r0.md) | **tedai 手代 — member-computer-operation Tier-B actor (R0)** — answers *「kotoba の actor が browser, computer 操作ができるような actor は設計している?」→「do it」*: closes the computer-operation gap (karakuri = web-service surface only; ameno runs actors, doesn't operate the desktop; tazuna = robot bodies; manimani reads, never actuates). karakuri's gate system lifted from the vendor-ToS axis to the **device-consent / surveillance / input-injection** axes, as a NEW sibling actor (the considered \"karakuri T2.5 desktop adapter\" rejected — different threat model). Uniform **DesktopOp** vocab (`app·noun·verb·safety·destructive·tier`; ServiceOp/ModelOp pattern) + the OS-layer **`:outward`** safety class (send/pay/post/upload held at the Council outward gate even WITH a member signature). Tiers: **T1 scripting/accessibility-API** (AppleScript/AX·UIA·AT-SPI·CLI) > **T2 stance-permitted vision-pointer** (computer-use shape; engine = **on-device vision** — baien edge/LAN Murakumo, **a screenshot never leaves the device**, G4) > **T3 file-level**; `:prohibited` synthetic-input stance (anti-cheat/DRM/banking) refuses T2 by construction, missing stance = default-deny; **browser apps route to karakuri** (N7, one owner per surface). Gates: G1 own-device-only/physically-paired (structurally not a RAT) · G2 stance-honest no-detection-evasion · G3 no-server-key (member-held pairing grant, member-signed mutate) · G5 read-default/mutate-gated/outward-held · G6 actuation-gated (R0 = plan/dry-run only; single live membrane refuses w/o env+operator+Council+member-sig, NotImplementedError at R0 even then) · G7 kotoba-EAVT audit · **G8 no-surveillance** (op-scoped own-session observation only; keylog/camera/mic/watch-user verbs **structurally unrepresentable** in t2_vision.py; never bossware) · **G9 evidence-minimization** (sha256-only, raw frame refused by the Datom projector). 5 cells (app_resolve/intent_plan/pairing_broker/actuate_invoke/evidence_audit, `.solve()` raises) + 4 methods + 5 Lexicons + :representative app registry; **113 tests green** (methods 79 + cells 34), stdlib-only. | proposed | 2026-06-10 |\n", :doc/path "90-docs/adr/README.edn", :doc/source-repo "root", :doc/topic "adr-readme", :doc/last_verified "2026-05-25", :doc/date "2026-05-25", :doc/authoritative true, :doc/related ["adr-2605170900-etzhayyim-root-adr-canonical-home"], :doc/authoritative_for ["ADR index for etzhayyim/root" "placement policy for open-scope ADRs"]}]
